    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d266-a2">

                <pb facs="0488" n="384" sameAs="frus:frus1890/pg384"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Tupper to Sir Julian Pauncefote.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >The Arlington</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1890-03-08"><hi rendition="#italic">March</hi> 8,
                        1890</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Sir Julian</hi>: I have the honor to inclose
                    herewith a memorandum prepared by me in reply to the memorandum sent to you by
                    Mr. Blaine, and which you handed to me upon the 3d instant.</p>
                <p>I send you a copy for yourself, one for Mr. Blaine, and one for M. de Struvé, the
                    Russian ambassador.</p>
                <p>I also have the honor to forward herewith a valuable paper upon the subject,
                    prepared hurriedly by the assistant director of the geological survey of Canada,
                    George Dawson, D. S., F. G. S., F. R. S. C., F. R. M. S.</p>
                <p>I may add that Dr. Dawson was in charge of the Yukon expedition in 1887.</p>
                <p>Copies of his paper are also inclosed for Mr. Blaine and M. de Struvé.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Charles H.
                    Tupper.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
